# `region r(4096)` as a STATEMENT (no colon) and `destroy r`.
#
# The parser was already giving this Stmt.Block("region", [strategy?], BINDING=name, [],
# line) — name in the BINDING slot, empty body — but the backend only lowered the BLOCK
# form and declined the statement form outright, which was the whole of the
# region_owned_structs baseline decline. Lowered as a named Arena local (lazy CHAINED
# backing; capacity presizing is an allocation-strategy detail, not observable behavior)
# pushed on the region unwind stack; `destroy` calls arena_free, which nulls begin/end so
# the return-path unwind's second free is a no-op.
def main() -> i64:
    region scratch(4096)
    xs: mutable darray[i64] @scratch = []
    xs.push(40)
    xs.push(2)
    out: i64 = xs[0] + xs[1]
    destroy scratch
    return out
